  "title": "Cowboy caviar",
  "description": "The jalapeño can be replaced by a few pinches of chili powder.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Cowboy caviar (or Texas caviar) is a simple, healthy,&nbsp;colorful, and delicious <span class=\"st\">appetizer</span>, salad,<span class=\"st\"> side-dish</span>, or <span class=\"st\">dip</span>. Using canned beans and corn is a quicker alternative to cooking dry beans. Spend less time in the kitchen but don't forget to prepare in advance to allow&nbsp;the different flavors to blend together before serving.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21346,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1770622674725} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21346-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Cowboy caviar</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/IMG_1990.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tThe jalapeño can be replaced by a few pinches of chili powder.\r\n\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>1  can (425 g) Black beans, Red beans, or Black Eye peas, or Tri-Bean blend (drained and rinsed)</li><li>1 can (425 g) whole kernel sweet corn (drained and rinsed)</li><li>1/2 red onion (peeled and minced)</li><li>1 bell pepper (red, yellow or orange) (cored and cubes)</li><li>1 jalapeño (cored and minced)</li><li>3 tomatoes (cubed)</li><li>1/4 bunch Fresh cilantro (chopped)</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</li><li>3 Tbsp apple cider vinegar (or lime juice)</li><li>4 Tbsp olive oil</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Combine all ingredients in a salad bowl, mix, cover, and let chill for about one hour in the fridge.</li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Salads</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
